SOAPBOX: 50W + low EFHW/Inv 'L'. Propagation was odd, lots of hollow, weak signals that had an auroral feel to them. Really struggled to get through to anyone much on Saturday, the piles were large and some quite unruly as callers were not listening to the op. LZ9W had some problems with key clicks on certain bands and was audible several kHz either side of the main signal (this was checked with 2 different receivers, FTdx109 & Airspy HF+ Discovery SDR, each on their own antenna). Seemed to improve on the Sunday. S & P activity only, but happy with 360 Qs and c125k points. Next year will have an antenna for 80m! 73 G3ESE (ex G4UCJ).
